; Arnold Games.db: settings a game starts with, found by the CRC-32 of its image.
;
; [CRC32] Title    CRC-32 of the cartridge (.cpr), the disk in drive A (.dsk) or the tape (.cdt)
;                  file, as 8 hex digits, then the title (a comment, shown in Arnold.log).
; key=value        the lines of a game's .prefs file: sound hires joykeys tall wide remap
;                  diskwrite fasttape tapesound rtg scanlines. They belong to the [..]
;                  line(s) above them.
;                  Several [..] lines in a row (other releases of the game) share the settings.
;
; Used only when the game has no <game>.prefs: Save for game (Game menu) always wins. The menu
; status line shows +db while these settings are in use. For a disk the ORIGINAL file is
; hashed (<disk>.bak if it exists), so a disk that has been written back still matches.
; Add your own: Arnold.log says "Games.db: ..." for a match; the CRC-32 of a file is also
; shown there ("Games.db: no entry for CRC ...") when a game has no entry.

[54B0034D] Sonic GX
wide=1

[E370FF4D] Pinball Dreams
tall=1
remap=RSHIFT:M

[AD9964F4] Bomb Jack GX
tall=1

[C8A699DE] R-Type (128K)
joykeys=3
wide=1
